DF32 Emulator based on NVRAM (by Charles E. Morris)
<UL>
<LI><b>writelockswitches</b> is a small board which has the write-lock
toggle switches.</LI>
<LI><b>DF32-revision-A</b> is Revision A of Charles' DF32 replacement, which
matches the prototype boards, but has known incompatibilities with the real
DF32.</LI>
<LI><b>busadapt-revision-A</b> is a little board to interface between the
Posibus paddles and the ribbon cables from the DF32 replacement.</LI>
<LI><b>DF32-revision-B</b> is Revision B of Charles' DF32 replacement, which
is meant to fix the compatibility bugs.</LI>
<LI><b>DEC8L-buscon</b> is Charles' version of the bus paddle, which isn't
quite compatible with anything but his DF32 replacement.</LI>
